# ===========================================================================
# .gitignore -- MoHQ cohort pipeline
#
# Two rules behind everything here:
#
#   1. NO PATIENT DATA, EVER. This is controlled-access human genomic data.
#      Git makes mistakes permanent: a file committed once stays in the
#      history even after it is deleted, and `git push` sends the whole
#      history. Removing it afterwards means rewriting history and
#      force-pushing, which is disruptive at best.
#
#   2. Nothing regenerable. Results, rendered reports and container images are
#      outputs of the code in this repo. Committing them bloats the history
#      (a rendered HTML report is >1 MB and changes completely on every knit)
#      and invites the question of which version is authoritative -- the file
#      or the code that made it.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Pipeline execution ---------------------------------------------------
work/
results/
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*
.nextflow.history*
timeline.html
report.html
trace.txt
dag.*

# --- PATIENT DATA. Do not relax these without asking the data steward. -----
# Persistent published artefacts. Every one contains variant-level data.
derived_mafs/
regenerated_pcgr/
filtered_ensemble/
collection/

# Manifests, completeness tables and audits: one row per patient, with
# absolute paths into the delivery tree.
audit/
.manifest_cache/
*.manifest.tsv
*.completeness.tsv
*.samples.tsv
*.ambiguities.tsv
mutation_provenance.tsv
# Audit outputs. Named for what they check, not for what they contain, which
# is why an earlier version of this file missed build_audit.tsv -- it matched
# none of the patterns above and was committed.
*audit*.tsv
*audit*.csv
build_audit.tsv
maf_annotation_audit.txt

# Raw data formats, wherever they land.
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.vcf.gz.tbi
*.tbi
*.maf
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.seg
*.cna_segments.tsv.gz

# The completeness inventory exports.
completeness*.csv
*completeness_live*.csv

# --- Regenerable outputs --------------------------------------------------
# Rendered reports. Keep the .Rmd; anyone can knit it.
reports/*.html
README.html
*_report.html
*_files/
*_cache/

# Container images -- hundreds of MB. Build from pipeline.def.
*.sif
*.simg

# --- Personal helpers, not part of the pipeline ---------------------------
bin/check_before_commit.sh

# --- Local noise ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
*.swp
*~
*.new
*.orig
*.bak

# --- Deliberately NOT ignored, for the record -----------------------------
# docs/*.svg, docs/*.png   -- the pipeline and completeness figures. Generated,
#                             but by scripts kept alongside them, small, and
#                             the thing people actually look at first.
# assets/*.tsv, *.csv      -- example samplesheet and cohort map. Synthetic.
# params/*.yaml            -- run configuration. Contains cluster paths but no
#                             patient data.
